/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# database
london.db
london.db-journal

# superpowers
.superpowers/

# The generated Prisma client IS committed. Prisma's Vercel guide recommends
# it for exactly this setup: "use a custom output path and check your client
# into version control. This way each deployment is guaranteed to include the
# correct Prisma Client." MongoDB needs the Rust query engine — there is no
# @prisma/adapter-mongodb, so the binary-free engineType="client" route is not
# available to us, and Prisma 7 (which drops the Rust engine) dropped MongoDB.
#
# Only the Linux engine is tracked. Each developer's native engine is rebuilt
# by the postinstall hook and would otherwise add ~18MB per platform.
/app/generated/prisma/*.node
!/app/generated/prisma/libquery_engine-rhel-openssl-3.0.x.so.node

# worktrees
.worktrees/

# local credential scratch copy — contains live API keys
copy.local

# stray scraper scratch files
/*.html
